extends ../../../layouts/master.pug

block title
  title NBC - Ministry Preparation Program

block header
  include ../../../components/header.pug

block content
  section.section-box
    .banner-hero.nav-breadcrums.bg-gray-100
      .container
        .breadcrumb
          ul
            li.home
              a(href='/index-4.html') Home
            li
              a(href='/programs/') Programs
            li
              span Ministry Preparation Program
  section.section-box
    .banner-hero.banner-head-image(style='background: url(/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_332409626.jpeg); background-size: cover; background-position: center bottom;')
      .container
        .text-center
          h1.text-heading-1.color-white.mt-30
            | Ministry Preparation Program
  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-50
    .container
      .content-detail
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            .box-quote
              | “… live a life worthy of the calling you have received. Be completely humble and gentle; be patient, bearing with one another in love. Make every effort to keep the unity of the Spirit through the bond of peace” (Ephesians 4:1−3).
              .box-user
                span.text-heading-5.color-white Ephesians 4:1−3
            p.text-body-text.mb-30
              | Ordination is an important part of ministry. Men and women who seek ordination as a pastor, elder, deacon or other ministry leader need to be well-prepared to answer their calling from the Lord.
            h2#overview.text-heading-5.text-center.mb-30 Are you prepared? Do you have a preparation plan?
            p.text-body-text
              | The Ministry Preparation Program (MPP) is designed to prepare men and women for ordination as an elder or deacon in the Church of the Nazarene. Those seeking ordination in other denominations may also find this helpful.
            p.text-body-text
              | MPP offers a series of courses that earn one semester hour of credit each. Two variations of the program exist:
              ul
                li
                  | 25-course ordination curriculum validated by the Regional and International Course of Study Advisory Committees (RCOSAC/ICOSAC) of the Church of the Nazarene as an approved curriculum for achieving ordination education requirements.
                li
                  | Modular program, which is likewise validated by RCOSAC/ICOSAC
            p.text-body-text
              | Students may choose which option they wish to pursue, pending the approval of their respective districts.

  section.section-box.overflow-visible.mb-100
    .container.mt-100
      .row
        .col-lg-10.mx-auto
          .bg-6.box-newsletter.position-relative
            .row
              .col-lg-5.col-md-7
                span.text-body-capitalized.color-gray-500.text-uppercase application
                h4.text-heading-2.mb-10.mt-10 Start moving forward with your ordination plan today.
                a.btn.btn-black.mt-50.mr-20(href='/tracks/elder/') Learn More
                a.btn.btn-black.mt-50.icon-arrow(href='/apply/') Apply
              .col-lg-7.col-md-5.mt-30.mt-lg-0.mt-md-30.mt-sm-30.position-relative.text-end
                img.img-responsive.img-newsletter(src='/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_968974436_vertical.jpeg', alt='Man sitting on stairs using a laptop')

  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-50
    .container
      .content-detail
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            p.text-body-text
              | Nazarene Bible College is approved by the Church of the Nazarene International Board of Education to train leaders toward ordination or commission in the ministries of the Church of the Nazarene. Individual districts in the Church of the Nazarene have autonomy in determining which courses fulfill their educational requirements for ordination.
            p.text-body-text
              | Completion of the MPP program does not guarantee ordination. Students should consult with their respective district ministry board or denomination to determine what courses are required for ordination.